mple: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.customer (Optional): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput} or null. Present only when `expand` includes `customer`; `null` when expanded and there is no related customer. object.customer.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput}. A customer's summary fields, returned in place of a customer ID when the customer is expanded. object.customer.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.customer_id (Required): string. The customer this subscription bills. Example: "cus_01KEZF7C006X9JK6NZNA2SM9XD". object.deliveries_per_period (Required): integer. Deliveries paid for by one billing period, from 1 to 24. One when no separate delivery cadence is set. Prices of lines that ship are per delivery. Format: int32. minimum: 1. maximum: 24. object.delivery (Optional): {@see SubscriptionDeliveryInput}. Saved delivery preference with the current delivery method display. Write responses use the same display as GET: fixed shipping reflects the current method configuration, and quoted shipping shows the last paid shipping amount when available. A subscription's saved delivery preference: method, destination, recipient, shipping cost, and who last changed it. object.delivery_hold (Optional): {@see SubscriptionDeliveryHoldInput}. Current delivery issue that blocks collection. Mutually exclusive with upcoming_delivery_hold. A hold on a subscription's deliveries because its delivery method or destination no longer works, and who can fix it. object.delivery_interval (Required): string or null. Delivery cadence frozen from the plan. Null when no separate delivery cadence is set; one delivery is made per billing period. Value enum: "daily", "weekly", "monthly", "yearly", null. object.delivery_interval_count (Required): integer or null. Number of delivery intervals between deliveries. Null when no separate delivery cadence is set. Format: int32. minimum: 1. object.early_termination_fee_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The fee in the recorded contract terms. Present whenever those terms include a fee. It applies only to a cancellation before contract_end_at. Flint never charges it. Later plan changes do not change this fee. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.end_after (Required): {@see SubscriptionEndAfterInput} or null. Recorded automatic end condition. Null when no automatic end is set. Cycles count charged billing periods, including imported completed_cycles. Pauses and skips do not use cycles. Already-paid prepaid deliveries continue on their shifted dates, even beyond the end date, and cancellation waits for the last remaining delivery. Skipping defers a delivery without consuming its entitlement. Ending never refunds. object.end_after.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see SubscriptionEndAfterInput}. The subscription's automatic end condition, measured by charged billing cycles or a saved local calendar date. object.end_after.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.expires_at (Required): string or null. Projected end under the current schedule and committed plan changes, including an earlier scheduled cancellation. A date limit preserves already-paid entitlement without requiring a future charge schedule. A reached cycle limit uses the last paid period end, or current_period_end_at when no paid history exists; that fallback includes any skip or pause extension. A cycle limit with cycles left needs a future charge schedule unless a known scheduled cancellation determines the end. Paid deliveries extend the end to the last paid delivery when it is later. An indefinite pause with paid deliveries owed makes the end unknown. Null when the end cannot be determined or the subscription is canceled. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.external_reference_id (Optional): string. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. maxLength: 255. Example: "warehouse-1842". object.gift_recipient (Required): {@see SubscriptionGiftRecipientInput} or null. Who receives the gift, when this is a gift subscription. customer_id stays the purchaser. Flint clears it when the subscription ends and when the purchaser's data is erased. Null when the subscription isn't a gift. object.gift_recipient.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see SubscriptionGiftRecipientInput}. Who receives a gift subscription. The customer stays the purchaser, who pays, gets receipts and reminders, and manages the subscription. delivery.recipient stays the ship-to address. object.gift_recipient.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.inventory_wait (Optional): {@see SubscriptionInventoryWaitInput}. Renewal waiting for stock. Buyers receive only started_at. Shows that a subscription renewal is waiting for inventory, with the order and invoice involved and when the wait started. object.is_awaiting_billing_schedule (Optional): boolean. True while an active or trialing subscription on an external billing schedule has no next billing date. object.last_payment_error (Optional): {@see PaymentErrorSummaryInput}. Latest renewal payment failure, present only while status is past_due and the latest payment failed. Buyer responses omit merchant remediation and sensitive decline signals. A summary of why a payment attempt failed, with a normalized error code, a message, the failure time, and remediation. object.line_items (Required): Array of {@see SubscriptionLineItemInput}. What each renewal bills. Plan edits do not change it. Adding, changing or swapping a line takes that variant's current catalog price, which then stays until the line changes again. object.line_items[] (Value): {@see SubscriptionLineItemInput}. An item included in a customer's recurring purchase. object.merchant_id (Required): string. ID of the merchant this resource belongs to. Example: "mer_01KEZF7C00KPYH1DDFPCCX3B6E". object.metadata (Optional): {@see MetadataMapInput}. Stored caller-owned key-value data. See `MetadataInput` for key, value, and size rules. Caller-owned key-value data stored on a resource. Keys starting with flint_ are reserved for Flint and are not returned. Writes follow the limits on MetadataInput and MetadataPatchInput; maps written before those limits may not satisfy them. object.missed_billing_at (Optional): string. The billing date whose payment failed, as an RFC3339 timestamp. Present only while status is past_due. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.next_billing_at (Optional): string. When Flint next starts a scheduled renewal charge, as an RFC3339 timestamp. Present only while a trialing or active subscription has a billing date and isn't set to cancel at the end of its period. Absent when no renewal is scheduled: a paused subscription resumes at scheduled_resume_at, a past_due one reports the failed billing date in missed_billing_at and retries at next_retry_at, an incomplete one retries at next_retry_at, a scheduled start begins at starts_at, one set to cancel ends at scheduled_cancel_at, and an external schedule awaiting a date reports is_awaiting_billing_schedule. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.next_delivery_at (Required): string or null. When the next prepaid delivery order is due, shifted by a timed pause. Null when the subscription has an indefinite pause, no delivery is scheduled, or the subscription is canceled. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.next_retry_at (Required): string or null. Recorded automatic payment retry time. Null when no retry time is available. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.open_renewal_order_id (Optional): string. ID of the paid renewal order whose shipment has not been dispatched. It keeps its committed delivery destination after preference changes and cancellation. Absent when no such renewal order exists. Only renewal orders count; the signup order is not included. Example: "ord_01KEZF7C0054GQKJ142A8X367A". object.outstanding_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Unpaid balance of the failed renewal order, includin